      "writtenOn": "2024-08-22T01:47:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This was a while ago, but I do recall lipfp and bep doing version checking differently and **would set/alter different global state differently**. I was pretty careful not to alter the behavior, even if I disagreed with it.\n\n---\n\n\u003e I didn\u0027t look to see if that would affect any other call sites, but maybe we can do the same thing.\n\nWe can, but IIRC we would need to rework a few functions, since `errors` is global state that is reported through fpinfo, I think.",
      "parentUuid": "79b8421d_ab931d50",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 130,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "38b144629c61b2ec68bd12aed5c6b2786e92e3a0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "756ef3df_11bd5823",
        "filename": "driver/fingerprint/fpc/libfp/fpc_private.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 133,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-10T23:03:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can\u0027t remember if there\u0027s a difference between `ASSERT` and `assert`. When compiling with the C standard library (like we do with fingerprint), defining `NDEBUG` will disable `assert`. IIRC, `ASSERT` is unconditional.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 133,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 133,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "38b144629c61b2ec68bd12aed5c6b2786e92e3a0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6a84ddeb_9f084a1e",
        "filename": "driver/fingerprint/fpc/libfp/fpc_private.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 133,
      "author": {
        "id": 1334530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-22T01:47:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, in the context of EC, I believe both can be disabled, but the hope is that we don\u0027t turn it off. This error is very unlikely.\n\nUndefining `CONFIG_DEBUG_ASSERT` will disable `ASSERT` and `assert`, if stdlib assert is not defined. If using stdlib, defining NDEBUG will be disable assert. I\u0027m not fully convinced that the stdlib assert implementation is what we want (I think it is a trap?), so I could be convinced to use ASSERT, instead.",
      "parentUuid": "756ef3df_11bd5823",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 133,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 133,
        "endChar": 7
      },
